From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Robinson <mrobinson@igalia.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:36:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deny: Accept unmaintained zbus-related crates (#48994)

We must accept these until our dependencies stop using them. In
particular these are used by `atspi-common`.

Testing: This should unblock the CI.

Signed-off-by: Martin Robinson <mrobinson@abandonedwig.info>
(cherry picked from commit 493d293e1947f8ebd9aed0b34c0393f0079838ef)

----

Fork note: backport of upstream 493d293e194 (#48994), which landed after
base/2026-10-13. RustSec marked zbus_names, zvariant and zvariant_derive
as unmaintained, so `cargo-deny` in the Lint job failed for every pull
request; they come in through `atspi-common`. The subject drops the
backticks of the upstream subject, which the stack manifest cannot
quote.
Drop at the next sync: every later base contains 493d293e194, so this
commit applies empty and becomes a `Superseded-by: 493d293e194`
placeholder (runbook decision 3).

Validation: `./mach test-tidy` on ohos-main 5ca16eccdc1 fails in `cargo-deny` with four advisories for rustls 0.23.45 and three unmaintained crates (zbus_names, zvariant, zvariant_derive), as the Lint job of every pull request does; with both backports, `cargo-deny` reports nothing. With both: `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`, the same with `--ohos` (SDK 6.1), and `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` (1150 tests) and `--doc` pass.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 493d293e194 without changes and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 deny.toml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deny.toml b/deny.toml
index 9198c7f72b4..900030e3f51 100644
--- a/deny.toml
+++ b/deny.toml
@@ -40,6 +40,15 @@ ignore = [
     # This is a dependency of `usvg`, `rustybuzz`, `fontdb`.
     # We will need to wait for upstream actions.
     "RUSTSEC-2026-0192",
+    # The crate `zvariant` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0370",
+    # The crate `zbus_names` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0371",
+    # The crate `zvariant_derive` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0372",
 ]
 
 # This section is considered when running `cargo deny check licenses`
